# Settings scripts/linux/run.sh reads for `play` and `prebuild` (and prints at
# the top of each log). One KEY=value per line, no quotes needed, nothing is
# run; a leading ~/ in a value is your home folder.
#
# Order, later wins:   this file  <  play.local.env  <  your shell's environment
# so `VICTORY_RELAY=2 scripts/linux/run.sh play` still changes one setting for
# one run. play.local.env (git-ignored, next to this file) is for your own
# paths and changes; start it from the example at the end of this file.

# --- Flamingo's tuned settings for an RTX 4070 (README "Playing") ----------
VICTORY_NO_WATCHDOG=1
VICTORY_PIPELINE_WAIT_MS=24
VICTORY_RELAY=1
VICTORY_CARD_BUFFERS_MIN_MB=1
# Flamingo 89e5d6c's settings (about 9-10 fps on Windows, RTX 4070): indirect
# windows off (clamping records ahead made characters lose parts), texture
# checks wide, other views of a page not guarded with it, textures picked by
# index uploaded by a thread of their own, and four broken shaders left out.
# Then the shaders whose pipelines vkd3d-proton/NVIDIA never finish making
# under Proton (each holds a pipeline worker for good; seen in our runs, and
# on AnyXboxX's Linux list): 32ed072b9f845048 fdd56d97a806bcca 17829ac71aab4e8d
# 559d9f0184e15fe3 a1b20bc47e3c9597 afeea48bbb9913ad e8c962358d862e3f, and
# AnyXboxX's 7f05ddab771799a9 a53a7977fe762268 be14e72d86362031.
VICTORY_INDIRECT_WINDOW=0
VICTORY_WIDE_TEXTURES=1
VICTORY_VIEW_GUARD=0
VICTORY_HEAP_WORKER=1
VICTORY_SKIP_PIPELINES=7115e46a79c78f98,59b1ba494f18c894,b8ca32a6899b87fb,659fe9cae59dbd88,32ed072b9f845048,fdd56d97a806bcca,17829ac71aab4e8d,559d9f0184e15fe3,a1b20bc47e3c9597,afeea48bbb9913ad,e8c962358d862e3f,7f05ddab771799a9,a53a7977fe762268,be14e72d86362031
# The shader clean-up passes draw black blocks. Part of the shader cache's
# key, so `prebuild` reads it too: both must agree or the warm-up is unused.
VICTORY_SHADER_OPT=0
VICTORY_WIDE_MERGE=1
# Constant ambient light; lower is darker, `off` for none.
VICTORY_AMBIENT=0.6

# --- Linux (Proton Experimental, RTX 4070 12 GB, 32 GB) ----------------------
# Under Wine the layer's bookkeeping of title memory (write watch, guards,
# copies) is most of a frame, not the GPU.
#
# Not set until measured on runs that draw (both were measured only on runs
# whose pipelines stopped being made, ~2,200 left "being made", a few draws a
# frame): VKD3D_CONFIG=force_host_cached, VICTORY_INPLACE=2 (suspected of that
# stall).
#
# Flamingo's Windows values are LATE_WAIT=3 and the wide copy-back on; under
# Wine they add copy-back work (AnyXboxX's Linux runs turn them off too).
VICTORY_LATE_WAIT=0
VICTORY_WIDE_BACK=0
# View memory stays known while its guard is open: the write watch is not
# asked about it, since it can only refuse (refused askings halved).
VICTORY_VIEW_KNOWN=1
# Series X: on Series S the game ran out of its own memory 9 minutes into the
# cutscene (Game Physical 98.6%). Series X wants more of the card: a smaller
# buffer pool, and textures up to 95% of the budget (not 90%).
FORK_PLAY_ARGS=--console series-x
VICTORY_CARD_BUFFERS_MB=512
VICTORY_TEXTURE_ROOM_PERCENT=95

# --- What the translation is made for (prebuild; play finds them itself) --
VICTORY_HOST_WAVE=32
VICTORY_VIEW_LIMIT=999999

# --- The NVIDIA driver's shader cache, for this game alone -------------------
# The driver keeps compiled shaders in ~/.cache/nvidia, shared with every other
# Vulkan/OpenGL program and trimmed to a small size by default: the title's
# thousands of pipelines push each other (and other games' shaders) out, and
# every launch compiles them again. Its own folder, capped at 10 GB (the driver
# still trims past the cap); delete the folder to start it over.
__GL_SHADER_DISK_CACHE_PATH=~/.local/share/flamingo-fork/nvidia-cache
__GL_SHADER_DISK_CACHE_SIZE=10737418240

# --- run.sh's own ----------------------------------------------------------
# Options for `victory.exe run` when `play` is given none: FORK_PLAY_ARGS,
# set above (`--console series-s` renders at 1280x720 with less memory).
# The title's executable, in its untouched dump folder: set it in
# play.local.env, then `scripts/linux/run.sh play` needs no path.
# FORK_GAME=~/Games/<the title>/<the title's exe>
# Scripted presses for runs nobody watches: `<seconds>:<key>,...` after input
# starts, each held 0.2 s with or without focus (Enter is the pad's A; also
# letters, digits, Esc, Tab, Back, Up, Down, Left, Right). The start screen's
# "press A" comes at a different time each launch, hence several presses.
# FORK_KEYS=30:Enter,45:Enter,60:Enter,90:Enter
# shaders.rpf for `prebuild` with no path (default: next to FORK_GAME).
# FORK_SHADERS=

# --- Example play.local.env --------------------------------------------------
# FORK_GAME=~/Games/<the title>/<the title's exe>
# VICTORY_SKIP_PIPELINES=
# MANGOHUD=1
